LOOPS:
Three important things to remember in loops:
1) Initialization - Initial value we are assigning.

2) Condition - when to stop the loop.

3) How are we going to update the value (Increase/Decrease).

eg: 
int i = 1; //Initialization
while(i<=3) //Condition
{
printf("hello");
i++; //increase/decrease
}

-Executes until the condition is "FALSE".

WHILE LOOP: SYNTAX

while(condition)
{
//statement
}
